== Equipment & Progression

Everything you earn from hunts funnels into one place: the smithy. Understand gear, and the whole game opens up.

=== Weapons

- *Forge* a new weapon, or *upgrade* an existing one along its tree. Upgrading is the main path — most weapons evolve through several forms.
- Weapons carry: attack, element/status, sharpness (melee), affinity (crit chance), and sometimes decoration slots.
- Two weapons of the same family can diverge — one raw, one elemental — so build for the matchup, not just "the strongest."
- Sunbreak adds *augment crafting* (Qurio Crafting) that upgrades weapons further — that is Part 5 territory.

=== Armor

- Armor's job is defense + *skills*. Every piece carries skill points; collect enough points of a skill and it activates at thresholds.
- *Upgrade armor* with armor spheres at the smithy — defense keeps up with the rank you are fighting. Under-leveled armor is the classic beginner death cause.
- *Sets vs mixed:* full sets are stylish and simple; mixing pieces lets you stack the skills you actually want. Wave 1 covers builds in depth.

=== Skills (The Real Power)

Skills are where gear becomes strategy. Early standouts that are almost never wasted:

- *Attack Boost* — flat damage; simple, always useful.
- *Weakness Exploit* — crit chance on weak spots; teaches you to aim.
- *Divine Blessing* — chunks incoming damage; the beginner's best friend.
- *Stun Resistance* — stops the stun death spiral.
- *Evade Window* — more invincibility frames on dodges.
- *Wirebug Whisperer* — more wirebugs to play with.

Every skill has levels; the effect grows at thresholds. Open any piece of armor and the skill list shows exactly what you have.

=== Decorations & Talismans

- *Decorations* are craftable gems that socket into armor slots. They are how you fine-tune a build: socket the skills you are missing.
- *Talismans* are equipable charms with random skills — obtained through *melding* at the smithy (trade materials for random talismans). Early on, use whatever fits; hunting for *the* talisman is endgame business (Part 5).

=== Money & Points

- *Zenny* — the currency. Earned from quest rewards; spent at the smithy. Sell spare materials when broke (the game warns you when a material is needed for something).
- *Kamura Points* — a second currency from gathering, subquests, and hunting. Spent at facilities: meal tickets, buddy gear, and trading.

=== Meals (Dango)

The canteen's dango is a before-every-hunt ritual: stat boosts (health, stamina, attack, defense) plus a *food skill* with a random proc chance. The skill rerolls each meal — if the proc you want does not show, order again.

#tip[
  Three habits that cover 90% of progression mistakes: eat dango every quest, upgrade armor every few quests, and craft/socket the skill that fixes whatever is killing you — not the skill that looks strongest on paper.
]
